---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
const guide = {
  "title": "US B1/B2 Visa from Pakistan: Application & Interview",
  "description": "Organise a US visitor application around the actual trip, DS-160, official fees and interview instructions without relying on approval promises.",
  "intro": "Organise a US visitor application around the actual trip, DS-160, official fees and interview instructions without relying on approval promises.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "US visitor visa guidance",
      "url": "https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas/tourism-visit/visitor.html"
    },
    {
      "title": "Interview wait times",
      "url": "https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas/visa-information-resources/global-visa-wait-times.html"
    },
    {
      "title": "US visa denials",
      "url": "https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas/visa-information-resources/visa-denials.html"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Check that the category fits",
      "paragraphs": [
        "B-1 covers permitted temporary business activities and B-2 covers tourism and visits. Ordinary employment and degree study need the appropriate separate route. Describe what you actually intend to do, rather than choosing a category that seems easier."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Prepare the file",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Complete DS-160, retain the confirmation and follow the responsible embassy’s booking and payment instructions. The published visitor application fee is USD 185; check any other applicable charges. Prepare the passport, photo requirements, receipt and relevant purpose, funding and departure evidence."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Make the plan consistent",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Put travel dates, accommodation and spending in one plan. Explain who pays and how the supporting evidence relates to the trip. Do not manufacture a profile by buying property or booking unrelated trips simply for visa purposes.",
        "The Department of State says an invitation or Affidavit of Support is not required for a visitor application and is not a deciding factor. Applicants qualify on their circumstances. Answer interview questions accurately instead of memorising a script."
      ],
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Check current appointment information",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Use the official table for the actual post and category. Interview estimates change and do not include every later processing step. Confirm current interview-waiver eligibility through official instructions rather than assuming previous approval removes the interview requirement."
      ],
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "heading": "Read the outcome",
      "paragraphs": [
        "A visa allows travel to request admission, not guaranteed entry or a guaranteed six-month stay. Follow the admission record after entry. If refused, identify the stated provision before deciding whether to provide more documents or start again."
      ],
      "source": 2
    }
  ]
};
---
<GuideLayout {...guide} />
